  "question": {
    "text": "The grid represents a region in space containing a uniform electric field <math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo> </math>each square of size&nbsp;<math><mtext>1m×1m</mtext></math><math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo> </math>. If potentials at point <math> <mtext>O</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>C</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>D</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>E</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>F</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>G</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>H</mtext> </math> are respectively <math> <mtext>0</mtext> </math>, <math> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mtext>1</mtext></mrow> </math>, <math> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mtext>2</mtext></mrow> </math>, <math> <mtext>1</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>2</mtext> </math>, <math> <mtext>0</mtext> </math>, <math> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mtext>1</mtext></mrow> </math>, <math> <mn>1</mn> </math> and <math> <mn>0</mn> </math> volts. find the electric field intensity.<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image11-16e37090-0541-4d88-a085-ef8e624b7e1d.jpg\" />",
